; WIT folds — every braced body, so a long `interface` collapses to its name.
;
; `world` and `interface` are the ones that matter in practice: a `wit/` package
; is mostly one long interface per file, and folding it is how you see the file's
; shape at all.
(world_item) @fold
(interface_item) @fold
(record_item) @fold
(enum_item) @fold
(variant_item) @fold
(flags_item) @fold
(resource_item) @fold
